   "lang": "python",
   "title": "static_triage.py — first look at a HARMLESS training file (complete, runnable)",
   "code": "import hashlib, math, re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef entropy(data):\n    if not data: return 0.0\n    counts = Counter(data); n = len(data)\n    return -sum((c/n) * math.log2(c/n) for c in counts.values())\n\nsample = b'TRAINING-SAMPLE CyberLab static analysis practice file. http://lab.invalid/beacon'\ndigest = hashlib.sha256(sample).hexdigest()\nstrings = re.findall(rb'[ -~]{5,}', sample)\nprint('sha256 :', digest[:32] + '...')\nprint('entropy:', round(entropy(sample), 2), '(plain text ~4-5; packed/encrypted often >7.2)')\nprint('strings:')\nfor s in strings: print('  ', s.decode())",
   "output": "sha256 : <first 32 hex of the digest>...\nentropy: ~4.5 (plain text ~4-5; packed/encrypted often >7.2)\nstrings:\n   TRAINING-SAMPLE CyberLab static analysis practice file. http://lab.invalid/beacon\n(One URL-shaped string is a lead for the report — in a real sample it is still only a lead until behavior confirms it.)",
